# gui/.xcode-version -- the Xcode whose build-setting presets are baked into
# the tracked project.pbxproj.
#
# FORMAT: marketing version, then the build version, whitespace separated.
# The BUILD is the operative one. See below.
#
# WHY THE BUILD AND NOT JUST THE MARKETING VERSION, MEASURED 2026-08-13.
#
# gui/.xcodegen-version pins the GENERATOR. It does not pin the generator's
# other input: xcodegen injects default build settings (settingPresets) that it
# reads from the SELECTED Xcode, so identical xcodegen + identical project.yml
# still emit different bytes on different Xcodes.
#
# The first version of this file pinned the marketing version, 26.6, on the
# theory that 26.6 emits COMBINE_HIDPI_IMAGES / LD_RUNPATH_SEARCH_PATHS /
# SDKROOT and older Xcodes omit them. That theory is FALSE, and the run that
# disproved it is worth keeping:
#
#   this Mac         xcodegen 2.44.1  Xcode 26.6 (17F113)  gate rc=0, PASS
#   macos-26 runner  xcodegen 2.44.1  Xcode 26.6 (?)       gate rc=1, three
#                                                          settings ABSENT
#
# Same generator. Same marketing version. Different bytes. So "26.6" does not
# identify a toolchain closely enough for a byte-exact comparison, and a gate
# pinned to it reports STALE for a difference the pin cannot see. That is the
# same defect the pin was added to prevent, one layer down, for the second
# time in this file.
#
# A mismatch here is UNAVAILABLE (exit 2), never STALE (exit 1).
#
# IF A RUNNER CANNOT SUPPLY THIS BUILD, that is the answer, not a failure to
# work around: a byte-exact comparison is only meaningful where the toolchain
# matches the machine that cuts the DMG. Do not relax the pin to make CI green.
# Move the byte comparison to the cut machine and give CI a check that does not
# depend on the toolchain.
26.6 17F113
